            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "2427bd44f85a68439a2c481bc989f05e9a4b57bd4eec7ff92430165ec4e9105d"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Take positive square order on the full scalar space",
          "text": "The shared auxiliary result applies to the positive operators γQ and Γ. Since (γQ)²=γ²Q, it gives Γ≥γQ. This is the operator-order step; a norm lower bound alone is not substituted for it.",
          "formula": "(\\gamma Q)^2\\le\\Gamma^2,\\quad\\gamma Q\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma\\ge0\\Rightarrow\\Gamma\\ge\\gamma Q.",
          "lean": "  have hOrder : (Γ-γ • Q).IsPositive :=\n    AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareOrder.positive_square_order\n      ν (γ • Q) Γ (hQpos.smul_of_nonneg hγ.le) hΓ hSquare\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/CenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "3c4f72ef44868fe2ebca6842192ee4a9cea1db4527ae29dccdec691004e6daa6",
            "start_line": 248,
            "end_line": 250,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "1fadde91d40827cb490ab5c651e07e96e51054f5414a55e1d606f249129c873c"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Restrict the same transported root to the exact centered space",
          "text": "The isometry identifies H_P^0 with zero ν-mean. Γ_P q_P=0 and selfadjointness preserve that closed kernel. Restrict Γ_P with inherited norm and inner product to Γ_0, and transport Γ≥γQ to Γ_0≥γI.",
          "formula": "H_P^0=\\ker\\langle q_P,\\cdot\\rangle,\\quad i_0\\Gamma_0=\\Gamma_Pi_0,\\quad\\Gamma_0\\ge\\gamma I.",
          "lean": "  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  have hCenter (f : HP) : f ∈ HP0 ↔ (∫ y,(e.symm f) y ∂ν)=0 := by\n    change inner ℝ (e q) f=0 ↔ _\n    rw [← e.apply_symm_apply f, e.inner_map_map,hq,e.symm_apply_apply]\n  have hΓPq : ΓP qP=0 := by\n    change e (Γ (e.symm (e q)))=0\n    rw [e.symm_apply_apply,hΓq,map_zero]\n  have hInv (f : HP0) : ΓP (f : HP) ∈ HP0 := by\n    change inner ℝ qP (ΓP (f : HP))=0\n    have hs : inner ℝ qP (ΓP (f : HP))=inner ℝ (ΓP qP) (f : HP) :=\n      (hΓP.inner_left_eq_inner_right qP (f : HP)).symm\n    rw [hs,hΓPq,inner_zero_left]\n  let ΓP0 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 := (ΓP.comp HP0.subtypeL).codRestrict HP0 hInv\n  have hΓP0 (f : HP0) : (ΓP0 f : HP)=ΓP (f : HP) := rfl\n  have hPos0 : ΓP0.IsPositive := by\n    refine ⟨?_,?_⟩\n    · intro f g\n      exact hΓP.isSymmetric (f : HP) (g : HP)\n    · intro f\n      exact hΓP.re_inner_nonneg_left (f : HP)\n  have hOrder0 : (ΓP0-γ • (1 : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0)).IsPositive := by\n    apply (ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_iff' _).mpr\n    refine ⟨hPos0.isSelfAdjoint.sub ((ContinuousLinearMap.isPositive_one).smul_of_nonneg hγ.le).isSelfAdjoint,?_⟩\n    intro f\n    let u : Lp ℝ 2 ν := e.symm (f : HP)\n    have hu : inner ℝ q u=0 := by rw [hq];exact (hCenter _).mp f.property\n    have hQu : Q u=u := by rw [hQ,hu,zero_smul,sub_zero]\n    have h := hOrder.inner_nonneg_left u\n    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.sub_apply,ContinuousLinearMap.smul_apply,\n      ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply,inner_sub_left,inner_smul_left,hQu] at h ⊢\n    have hInner : inner ℝ (ΓP0 f) f=inner ℝ (Γ u) u := by\n      change inner ℝ (ΓP (f : HP)) (f : HP)=_\n      change inner ℝ (e (Γ u)) (f : HP)=_\n      rw [← e.apply_symm_apply (f : HP),e.inner_map_map]\n    rw [hInner]\n    have hNorm : inner ℝ f f=inner ℝ u u := by\n      change inner ℝ (f : HP) (f : HP)=_\n      rw [← e.apply_symm_apply (f : HP),e.inner_map_map]\n    rw [hNorm]\n    exact h\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/CenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "3c4f72ef44868fe2ebca6842192ee4a9cea1db4527ae29dccdec691004e6daa6",
            "start_line": 251,
            "end_line": 293,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "3d8c6caa45f0b69bddc0db96cd40a2acef1e3198bf15936b99b8d0b36a094afe"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive an actual bounded inverse",
          "text": "The quadratic bound gives γ‖f‖²≤⟨Γ_0f,f⟩. With γ>0, the complete-Hilbert coercivity result proves that Γ_0 is a unit; injectivity, closed range and dense range are internally established by that theorem.",
          "formula": "\\gamma\\|f\\|^2\\le\\langle\\Gamma_0f,f\\rangle\\Rightarrow \\Gamma_0\\in\\mathcal B(H_P^0)^\\times.",
          "lean": "  have hCoerc (f : HP0) : γ*‖f‖^2 ≤ inner ℝ (ΓP0 f) f := by\n    have h := hOrder0.inner_nonneg_left f\n    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.sub_apply,ContinuousLinearMap.smul_apply,\n      ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply,inner_sub_left,inner_smul_left,real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq,\n      starRingEnd_apply,star_trivial] at h\n    linarith\n  have hUnit : IsUnit ΓP0 := by\n    apply ContinuousLinearMap.isUnit_of_forall_le_norm_inner_map ΓP0 (c:=⟨γ,hγ.le⟩) hγ\n    intro f\n    have hnn : 0 ≤ inner ℝ (ΓP0 f) f := hPos0.inner_nonneg_left f\n    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs,abs_of_nonneg hnn,mul_comm]\n    exact hCoerc f\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/CenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "3c4f72ef44868fe2ebca6842192ee4a9cea1db4527ae29dccdec691004e6daa6",
            "start_line": 294,
            "end_line": 305,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "1d3a43a8fb680d214552f352eabca0b640aba9e5a7d6bf0c9f74d646758388e5"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove both cancellations and the accurate inverse norm",
          "text": "Take the inverse of the derived unit and prove both products equal the identity by application congruence. Cauchy–Schwarz gives γ‖f‖≤‖Γ_0f‖; substitute f=Inv g to obtain ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. The full-space constant kernel is kept separate.",
          "formula": "\\mathrm{Inv}\\,\\Gamma_0=\\Gamma_0\\,\\mathrm{Inv}=I,\\quad\\|\\mathrm{Inv}\\|\\le\\gamma^{-1}=\\frac{1+\\alpha\\eta}{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}.",
          "lean": "  let Inv : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 := ↑(hUnit.unit⁻¹)\n  have hLeft : Inv*ΓP0=1 := by\n    exact (congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => Inv*C) hUnit.unit_spec).symm.trans\n      (Units.inv_mul hUnit.unit)\n  have hRight : ΓP0*Inv=1 := by\n    exact (congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C*Inv) hUnit.unit_spec).symm.trans\n      (Units.mul_inv hUnit.unit)\n  have hNormCoerc (f : HP0) : γ*‖f‖ ≤ ‖ΓP0 f‖ := by\n    by_cases hf : f=0\n    · simp [hf]\n    · have hn : 0 < ‖f‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr hf\n      have h := (hCoerc f).trans (by\n        calc inner ℝ (ΓP0 f) f ≤ ‖inner ℝ (ΓP0 f) f‖ := le_abs_self _\n             _ ≤ ‖ΓP0 f‖*‖f‖ := norm_inner_le_norm _ _)\n      nlinarith [h]\n  have hNormInv : ‖Inv‖ ≤ 1/γ := by\n    apply Inv.opNorm_le_bound (show 0≤1/γ from by positivity)\n    intro f\n    have h := hNormCoerc (Inv f)\n    have hc : ΓP0 (Inv f)=f := congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C f) hRight\n    rw [hc] at h\n    have hh : ‖Inv f‖ ≤ ‖f‖/γ := (le_div_iff₀ hγ).mpr (by simpa only [mul_comm] using h)\n    simpa only [one_div,div_eq_mul_inv,mul_comm,one_mul] using hh\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/CenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "3c4f72ef44868fe2ebca6842192ee4a9cea1db4527ae29dccdec691004e6daa6",
            "start_line": 306,
            "end_line": 328,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "ceab762484db001dc0353b896d5854fb87c99ef4ca64acf919609c8acd2ca360"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Exercise the normalized actual leakage consumer",
          "text": "The Test starts from the original potential/Hessian/step inputs. The SAME Gram identity and Γ_0Inv=I give ‖B i_0 Inv f‖=‖f‖, and PB=0 puts this actual leakage in ker P. No gap, unit, inverse, isometry or expected-cost premise is supplied. This Test does not publish a full polar/onto theorem.",
          "formula": "\\|B i_0\\mathrm{Inv}f\\|=\\|f\\|,\\quad P B i_0\\mathrm{Inv}f=0.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hBase := AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.CenteredRootOrderInverse.actual_centered_root_order_inverse\n    (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  dsimp only at hBase\n  rcases hBase with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,\n      T,hTs,hAll,hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,\n      Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv⟩\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  have hGramLocal : B.adjoint ∘L B=ΓP*ΓP := hGram\n  have hPosLocal : ΓP.IsPositive := hΓP\n  refine ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,T,hTs,hAll,\n    hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,\n    ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv,?_⟩\n  intro f\n  let g : HP0 := Inv f\n  have hg : ΓP0 g=f := congrArg (fun C : HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 => C f) hRight\n  have hb := B.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right (g : HP)\n  have hr := ΓP.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right (g : HP)\n  rw [hGramLocal] at hb\n  rw [hPosLocal.isSelfAdjoint.adjoint_eq] at hr\n  have hNorm : ‖B (g : HP)‖=‖ΓP (g : HP)‖ :=\n    (sq_eq_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)).mp (hb.trans hr.symm)\n  refine ⟨?_,hPB (g : HP)⟩\n  calc\n    ‖B (HP0.subtypeL (Inv f))‖=‖ΓP (g : HP)‖ := hNorm\n    _ = ‖ΓP0 g‖ := congrArg (fun z : HP => ‖z‖) (hΓP0 g).symm\n    _ = ‖f‖ := congrArg (fun z : HP0 => ‖z‖) hg\n",
          "detail": "Literal excerpt of the compiled declaration; preceding local definitions and proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "Tests/ProximalBPSCenteredRootOrderInverse.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "fd265a79bfbf770f4c4fa3fdc6511b9e9e35cb970597787d910740548a69a60a",
            "start_line": 86,
            "end_line": 134,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "2ae8f57ae86b7a2d712befd9db36efc2f2eb0e29a8feecda2eea9b01c1c8e089"
          }
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted.",
      "lean_proof": "Keep the actual objects and identify the constant kernel; Join the same gradient graph and same conditional mean; Derive the sharp centered contraction and exact constant; Use the scalar constant-complement projection; Take positive square order on the full scalar space; Restrict the same transported root to the exact centered space; Derive an actual bounded inverse; Prove both cancellations and the accurate inverse norm; Exercise the normalized actual leakage consumer",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicDefectRoot.actual_unique_positive_macroscopic_defect_root",
